Package: gnome-shell-extension-power-only-quicksettings
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 gnome-shell (>= 48~),
 gnome-shell (<< 51~)
Description: GNOME Shell extension that shows only a power icon in the top bar
 Hides every status icon in the Quick Settings area of the top bar except a
 single power icon. Clicking it still opens the full Quick Settings panel.
 Icons that GNOME Shell shows again later, for example when the microphone
 goes live, are hidden again. Disabling the extension puts every icon back as
 it was.
 .
 After installing, log out and back in once, then enable it with
 `gnome-extensions enable power-only-quicksettings@spencercnorton.github.io`.
